  "2026-10-20T16:44:57.196Z",codex-agent,"Review round for PR #134: fetched all thread and comment pages; only unresolved thread is PRRT_kwDOToJT7M6uafK2. Latest substantive CodeRabbit review has no Outside diff range findings. Remote head is current and main is already included. Plan: bounded receiver-local positive closure receipts, invalidated on policy changes and future revocation deadlines; retain independent object-closure validation and publication lease. Add behavioral regressions, prove failures with the changed function reverted, self-review all signing/publication boundaries, rebuild and run unchanged npm and Bun release gates."
  "2026-10-20T16:49:29.644Z",codex-agent,"Implemented native-engine positive closure receipts (16 receivers, 4096 boundaries each), exact-policy invalidation, scheduled-revocation expiry and final-clock revalidation. Complete object closure validation remains mandatory. Self-review covered signing payloads, rewrite invalidation, detached HEAD replay, clone policy isolation, direct/resumable publication and forge publication; no additional valid defect found. Revert proof: replacing only assertTrustedChanges with its pre-round implementation, leaving new tests and cache helper intact, makes node --test --test-name-pattern \"publication stops at receiver-verified history\" test/signatures.test.ts fail (1 test, 0 pass, 1 fail; expected warm decoded-commit visits 0, actual 1). Restored the fixed function. Initial focused suite 33/33 passed; lint, 0-percent duplication and docstrings passed. Final regressions also cover a real non-Git tracker and cached-tip object corruption."
  "2026-10-20T16:51:43.246Z",codex-agent,"Linked pinned-pm test node --test test/signatures.test.ts test/publication-validation.test.ts passed 40/40 with zero failures/cancellations/skips/todos. Existing tracker policy disables persisted test-result storage; receipts are documented here without changing policy. Measured 2000-change signature publication: cold 1119.514 ms, cached 0.412 ms and zero decoded-commit visits (host-dependent measurement). Self-review additionally requires cache invalidation after receiver clock rollback. Removing only the two rollback guards makes node --test --test-name-pattern \"receiver clock rollback\" test/signatures.test.ts fail 0/1 (expected one revalidation visit, actual zero). Restored guards; targeted expiry/rollback suite passes 3/3. Final linked rerun includes that new test. Original history remains append-only."
